window.docContents[104].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Kernel.Sys/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Kernel___Sys":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Kernel › Sys.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 50 of 85 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (8)def SYS_SET_TID_ADDRESSdef SYS_SCHED_GETAFFINITYdef SYS_GETPIDdef SYS_GETTIDdef SCHED_AFFINITY_MASKdef execSetTidAddressdef execGetpiddef execSchedGetaffinity\n\nThread Identity and Affinity SyscallsLinux AArch64 syscall numbers and transition functions for set_tid_address (96), sched_getaffinity (123), getpid (172), and gettid (178), modeled after Linux kernel/fork.c, kernel/sched/syscalls.c, and kernel/sys.c in a single-process, single-thread, single-CPU environment.\n\n\n\ndef SYS_SET_TID_ADDRESSL27–28 ↗#Linux AArch64 set_tid_address syscall number (__NR_set_tid_address = 96, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:278, kernel/fork.c:1866).\n\ndef SYS_SCHED_GETAFFINITYL30–31 ↗#Linux AArch64 sched_getaffinity syscall number (__NR_sched_getaffinity = 123, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:344, kernel/sched/syscalls.c:1395).\n\ndef SYS_GETPIDL33–34 ↗#Linux AArch64 getpid syscall number (__NR_getpid = 172, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:472, kernel/sys.c:966).\n\ndef SYS_GETTIDL36–37 ↗#Linux AArch64 gettid syscall number (__NR_gettid = 178, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:487, kernel/sys.c:979).\n\ndef SCHED_AFFINITY_MASKL39–41 ↗#8-byte kernel cpumask_t (CPU 0 online) written by sched_getaffinity.\n\ndef execSetTidAddressL43–48 ↗#set_tid_address(tidptr) (__NR_set_tid_address = 96, kernel/fork.c:1866): per Linux kernel/fork.c, records clear_child_tid ([INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: no-op in single-threaded execution without CLONE_CHILD_CLEARTID) without dereferencing tidptr, and always succeeds returning the caller's thread ID (SIM_TID = 1).\n\ndef execGetpidL50–54 ↗#getpid() (__NR_getpid = 172, kernel/sys.c:966) and gettid() (__NR_gettid = 178, kernel/sys.c:979): return the calling process/thread ID (SIM_TID = 1) in the single-process, single-thread model ([INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]).\n\ndef execSchedGetaffinityL56–86 ↗#sched_getaffinity(pid, cpusetsize, mask) (__NR_sched_getaffinity = 123, kernel/sched/syscalls.c:1278,1307 SYSCALL_DEFINE3(sched_getaffinity, pid_t, pid, unsigned int, len, unsigned long __user *, user_mask_ptr) -> sched_getaffinity -> find_process_by_pid at kernel/sched/syscalls.c:215): models Linux kernel/sched/syscalls.c on a single-CPU AArch64 system (cpumask_size() = 8, sizeof(unsigned long) = 8, CPU 0 online):* if 32-bit unsigned int cpusetsize < 8 or cpusetsize % 8 != 0, returns -EINVAL;* if (pid : Int32) < 0 (pid.slt 0#32), returns -ESRCH (find_process_by_pid(pid) returns NULL in kernel/sched/syscalls.c:1284-1286);* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: if pid != 0 (calling thread) and pid != 1 (SIM_TID), fails closed with .Exception \"unmodeled sched_getaffinity pid\";* if !s.mem.canWrite mask 8, returns EFAULT_RET (-EFAULT);* otherwise writes the 8-byte single-CPU mask (SCHED_AFFINITY_MASK) to mask and returns 8 (cpumask_size()).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Kernel/Sys.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Kernel.Sys/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Kernel___Sys"}});